# Keeping the build context to the sources the image is built from: everything else only slows the
# build and, for bin/obj, risks host artifacts (Windows paths, a different RID) leaking into it.
**/bin/
**/obj/
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vs/
.vscode/
.worktrees/
docs/
tests/
tools/
api-client/
logs/
**/*.user
**/*.DotSettings.user
# Every environment file: the Web API's own Environments folder (the container is configured from its
# environment, and a file copied into the image would be loaded ahead of nothing useful -- at best
# placeholders, at worst values from another machine) and the per-environment Compose files, which
# hold this deployment's real secrets and have no business inside a built image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
docker/*.env
!.config/dotnet-tools.json
